WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.370
The 2017 film version of Stephen King's It
made its mark as one of the biggest critical

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:09.730
and commercial hits of the year, but it wasn't
the first time the horror master's classic

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:12.500
1986 story made its way to the screen.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:17.730
The book's original adaptation, a 1990 TV
miniseries, lacked a movie-sized budget and

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:21.930
modern special effects, but it still managed
to give audiences plenty of scares.

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:26.529
The TV version of It had a strong cast going
for it, including budding young stars and

00:00:26.529 --> 00:00:29.429
formidable character actors portraying the
adults.

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:33.470
With the exception of Jonathan Brandis and
John Ritter, who've passed away since the

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:38.270
movie's release, most of It's original cast
is still busy with strong Hollywood careers.

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:42.750
Here's a look back at the original ensemble
and what they've been up to in the 27 years

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:44.700
since Pennywise last reared his head.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:46.620
Richard Thomas

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:51.150
TV fans might best remember Richard Thomas
for his Emmy-winning turn as "John-Boy" in

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:51.780
the The Waltons.

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:56.200
But for horror fans, Richard Thomas will always
be remembered as the grownup version of Bill

00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:00.550
Denbrough, taking over the role of the Losers'
leader from Jonathan Brandis.

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:05.489
After It, Thomas continued his prolific acting
career with more films like Wonder Boys and

00:01:05.489 --> 00:01:07.400
TV series such as The Americans.

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:12.620
Thomas also maintains a steady career on the
stage, recently earning a Tony Award nomination

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:16.300
for his role in the 2017 Broadway revival
of The Little Foxes.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:17.600
Brandon Crane

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:23.071
In the 1990 miniseries, Brandon Crane played
the young version of Ben Hanscom, who was

00:01:23.071 --> 00:01:27.009
frequently bullied by Henry Bowers and his
gang because of his weight.

00:01:27.009 --> 00:01:31.409
Around the same time, Crane also had a recurring
role on the classic drama-comedy series The

00:01:31.409 --> 00:01:34.100
Wonder Years as Kevin's close friend Doug
Porter.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:39.179
Following his appearance in It, Crane continued
to appear on the small screen and in short

00:01:39.179 --> 00:01:43.729
films, and these days he makes his living
as a stage actor, singer, and front-end website

00:01:43.729 --> 00:01:44.229
developer.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:49.000
During the summer of 2017, Crane reunited
with some of the other Derry alums to film

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.480
the upcoming documentary, Pennywise: The Story
of 'IT.'

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:54.060
Emily Perkins

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:59.299
Canadian actress Emily Perkins portrayed the
young version of Beverly Marsh in the miniseries,

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:01.020
and it was one of her first major roles.

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:05.200
But something about her stint as a scream
queen in It seemed to stick, because she would

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:09.560
later continue to star in scary projects like
The X-Files and and Ginger Snaps.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:14.260
Nowadays, she's taking a break from the small
screen as she enjoys her newest role as mom.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:15.840
Annette O'Toole

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:20.540
Before she became the adult Beverly Marsh
in It, Annette O'Toole appeared as Clark Kent's

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:23.220
love interest Lana Lang in Superman III.

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:28.040
And after defeating the Derry demon, O'Toole
returned to the Smallville fold by starring

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:30.020
as the Superman's mother on the small screen.

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:34.360
After that was done, however, she came back
to the realm of Stephen King for a brief stint

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:37.700
on the small screen adaptation of 11.22.63.

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:38.860
Seth Green

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:43.650
Long before he became a household name, Seth
Green was the foul-mouthed wisecracking Richie

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:45.380
Tozier in the It miniseries.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:49.980
He later rose to fame with roles in the Austin
Powers film franchise, his long-running role

00:02:49.989 --> 00:02:54.579
as Oz on Buffy the Vampire Slayer, and the
dozens of other films and TV shows he's been

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:55.100
a part of.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:59.700
Nowadays, his steadiest work seems to happen
behind a microphone: he provides voices for

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:04.320
Family Guy, Robot Chicken and Teenage Mutant
Ninja Turtles, and even made into the Marvel

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:08.180
Universe as the voice of Howard the Duck in
the Guardians of the Galaxy movies.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:09.460
Harry Anderson

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:14.040
For adult Richie, actor-comedian Harry Anderson
stepped into the role.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.740
"Beep beep Richie" "I didn't hear that."

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:21.840
Anderson is likely better known for his long-running
role as Judge Harry Stone in the NBC sitcom

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:26.580
Night Court, but he's also popped up in popular
series like Cheers and Hearts Afire.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:31.400
But much like Richie, he's always had comedy
at heart, and these days, he can be seen performing

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:34.220
stand-up routines and magic shows around the
country.

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:35.700
Adam Faraizl

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:40.040
Twelve-year-old Eddie Kaspbrak 
was the most timid member of the Losers' Club,

00:03:40.049 --> 00:03:44.440
frequently jumping at his own shadow or complaining
of ailments, like asthma, that his mother

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:45.700
convinced him he suffered from.

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:51.240
Playing Eddie in the 1990 miniseries was Adam
Faraizl, who didn't stick with acting for

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:53.140
long after It premiered on television.

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:58.170
He made a handful of appearances in TV movies
like Where the Red Fern Grows, but ultimately

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:03.400
he found a professional passion in the restaurant
business where he specializes in bar beverages.

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:04.640
Dennis Christopher

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:09.579
Playing the adult version of Eddie Kaspbrak
in the It miniseries was Dennis Christopher,

00:04:09.579 --> 00:04:14.480
who first rose to prominence in Hollywood
with his starring role as Dave in the 1979

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:15.300
film Breaking Away.

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:19.920
Christopher went on to appear in many more
films and television shows over the years,

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:22.190
including Roswell and Star Trek: Enterprise.

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:26.710
He also appeared in Quentin Tarantino's Django
Unchained and recently starred in several

00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:29.360
episodes of the Epix comedy series Graves.

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:30.900
Marlon Taylor

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:35.830
Playing young Mike Hanlon was actor Marlon
Taylor, who also appeared in a handful of

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:39.520
other television roles as a child, including
Sister, Sister.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:45.130
After 1994, Taylor took a hiatus from acting,
but reappeared in 2009 when he co-starred

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:47.310
in the rap drama Know Thy Enemy.

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:51.060
Information about what he's been up to since
then is scarce, but according to Taylor's

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:56.060
Twitter account, he recently finished filming
a part for an episode in season four of Syfy's

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:58.420
post-apocalyptic TV series Z-Nation.

00:04:58.840 --> 00:04:59.600
Tim Reid

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:04.160
Tim Reid played out the rest of Mike Hanlon's
tale for viewers, as he discovers that It

00:05:04.169 --> 00:05:07.349
has returned 27 years after their last encounter.

00:05:07.349 --> 00:05:11.960
Like his younger counterpart Marlon Taylor,
Tim Reid also appeared on the sitcom Sister,

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:16.280
Sister and continued to act in a number of
films and television shows, including That

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:18.220
'70s Show and Treme.

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:22.930
Most recently, Reid made a couple of appearances
as Bishop Lionel Jeffries in the Oprah Winfrey

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:24.560
Network drama series Greenleaf.

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:26.000
Ben Heller

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:30.380
Being an actor isn't for everyone, and it
certainly seems that was the case for Ben

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:34.700
Heller, who played the 12-year-old version
of Stanley Uris in 1990.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:38.260
Stan is the most logical — and skeptical
— of the Losers' Club members, and Heller

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:39.640
handled the role just fine.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:43.300
However, his appearance as Stan was his first
and last acting role.

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:47.160
Fans will get to finally find out what he's
been up to in his post-Derry days when he

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:50.940
appears on the 2018 documentary about the
mini-series' production.

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:52.480
Richard Masur

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:56.460
Stan was the one who initiated the blood oath
between the Losers' Club members when they

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:57.180
were children.

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:00.820
But when he learns that he'll have to make
good on that promise, his fear of facing the

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:03.280
ancient evil again leads him to take his own
life.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:04.220
"Sorry I'm late."

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:08.740
Richard Masur is probably better known for
his work in shows like Rhoda and films like

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:09.260
The Thing.

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:13.560
Today, he's still a regular on the small screen,
having recently starred in The Good Wife and

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:15.040
Orange is the New Black.

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:16.500
Tim Curry

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:21.920
Renowned actor Tim Curry did much of the heavy
lifting in the 1990 It miniseries with his

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:24.169
role as Pennywise the Dancing Clown.

00:06:24.169 --> 00:06:28.569
While there has been considerable buzz surrounding
Bill Skarsgård's modern take on the character

00:06:28.569 --> 00:06:33.530
in the 2017 film adaptation, it still doesn't
displace Curry's cheeky performance as a fan

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:35.620
favorite from the first adaptation.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:40.340
Following It, Curry continued his extremely
prolific acting career with dozens of roles

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:42.140
in films and television shows.

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:47.280
And even after suffering a stroke in 2012
which left him wheelchair-bound, Curry refused

00:06:47.289 --> 00:06:51.860
to slow down, taking a voice role in Star
Wars: The Clone Wars and returning to The

00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:56.320
Rocky Horror Picture Show realm as the Criminologist
in the Fox TV remake.

00:06:56.320 --> 00:06:59.460
And he's still ready to bust out Pennywise
whenever the need arises:

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:05.440
"And we say down here we float."

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:06.780
Thanks for watching!

00:07:06.789 --> 00:07:09.540
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:11.840
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

